description:
Função: 

Integração na equipa de Data Scientists e participação no desenvolvimento e entrega de múltiplos projetos estratégicos para clientes transformando dados em conhecimento através de variadas técnicas complexas. 

Competências: 

- Formação Superior nas áreas de Economia, Estatística, Matemática, Ciência da Computação, Sistemas de Informação ou outra área similar; 

- Experiência mínima de 3 anos em desenvolvimento de soluções/projetos de IT; 

- Experiência e Conhecimentos Sólidos em: 

Modelação de Dados; 

SQL e PL/SQL (criação e otimização de Queries e procedimentos complexos); 

Desenvolvimento de processos de ETL (preferencialmente em IBM SPSS Modeler ou Powercenter); 

Dinamização de Dashboards em Microsoft Power BI (ou Qlikview, SAP BusinessObjects BI ou Tableau). 

- Capacidade de manter e gerir a comunicação com o cliente (entender as suas necessidades de negócio e desenhar requisitos funcionais que vão de encontro às mesmas); 

- Capacidade de adaptação a um contexto/cliente difícil, com uma enorme complexidade de fontes de dados e foco na resolução de problemas; 

- Conhecimento que permita a análise, a especificação e o desenho de soluções num interface web que vão de encontro às necessidades do cliente (em conjunto com os developers da equipa); 

- Pensamento criativo e gosto por dados, análise de dados e soluções de Business Intelligence; 

- Capacidade produzir documentação inerente aos projetos (especificações de requisitos funcionais, documentos de início de projeto, cadernos de arquitetura, testes de aceitação, entre outros); 

- Boa capacidade de comunicação e facilidade em trabalhar em equipa; 

- Autonomia no desenvolvimento das tarefas; 

- Fluência em Inglês (falado e escrito). 

Extras: 

- Experiência e conhecimento básico sobre análise de dados em deteção de fraude; 

- Conhecimentos de ferramentas de análises de dados; 

- Fluência em diversos idiomas.

Dockstr is looking for an ambitious SENIOR FULL-STACK REMOTE DEVELOPER professional with an entrepreneurial spirit. Someone excited for a new challenge where you would have the space to grow and make an impact. You should be comfortable operating in an international and fast paced environment where you can become a valuable member of our team.

This is for a PART-TIME position initially but it may evolved over time to a full time position.

RESPONSIBILITIES:
- Lead a number of product development areas;
- Contribute to taking our existing technical solutions to the next level;
- Take a leading role in the area of UX, UI and front-end development of our solutions;
- When it comes to UX/UI, you will help us to bring together exceptional design, creativity and usability;
- Play a key role in building our tech team for the future and setting the team culture to deliver products that exceed expectations.

OUR STACK:
- Frontend: JS, React, Apollo, GraphQL, SASS, Material UI
- Server: Ruby, Ruby on Rails, Elasticsearch, Redis, AWS S3
- Tools and services: Github, Slack

WE ARE LOOKING FOR AN ENGINEER WITH:
- 5-7 years of experience in designing, building Ruby on Rails applications;
- Proﬁciency in front-end and back-end development;
- Track-record of continuous integration and delivery;
- Familiarity with Heroku and Postgres;
- Fluency in English;
- Creative, ﬂexible, and meticulous working style.

SET-UP:
- Remote;
- Part-time - between 40 to 80 hours a month initially.

The potential for you to grow with us and to inﬂuence our direction is not insignificant. So if you’re a confident developer, wondering where you could achieve maximum impact, why not consider working with one of the best early-stage startups in Scandinavia and put your skills/experience into action. 

If you think your proﬁle, capabilities and ambition match our plans then ping us and let’s talk!

Scope is extremely specific, and the turnaround times is extremely tight. Looking for a skilled developer that has experience with Django REST Framework in a production environment where Django is running on a Linux Server with Nginx and Gunicorn. Our Linux Server is currently running on EC2 in AWS and we’re leveraging a S3 bucket to store images via POST Request from the client (iPhone) via the below API through s3boto3. All other data is stored in PostgreSQL. The ideal candidate will have experience with the above-mentioned architecture. At a minimum the candidate MUST have experience with Django REST Framework in a production environment where Django is running on a Linux Server with Nginx and Gunicorn.

As mentioned above, looking to expound on the else condition in the below API to return more information when experiencing unsuccessful POSTs (other than 201). What we currently have doesn’t tell us much about the issue. Sometimes it works and sometimes it doesn't. We need a traceback implemented to determine if the issue is with Django application or s3boto3. The traceback data must have a date and timestamp associated with it and stored as a separate file on the Linux server. Traceback must have data in the sterilizer attached, so we can identify what entries failed and why. 

While we understand that this scope is limited, the ideal candidate will be used for additional follow-up work regarding our production Django application.

See attached document for urls, API (below) and serializer

